original_description_sprint:
When creating a Async pipeline sometimes QFuture.then() may return QFuture. It's useful to unwrap the returned QFuture such there's not QFuture<QFuture<T>>. For example: auto download = [](QUrl url) {
   ...
   return QList<Tile>({tile1, ..., tileX});
}

auto processTiles = [](QList<Tile> tiles) {
   QFuture<QImage> future = QtConcurrent::mappedReduced(tiles, 
                                             processTile, //Map function
                                             reduceTiles) //Reduce function
   return future;
} 

auto saveImage = [](QImage image) {
   image.save(...);
}

auto future = QtConcurrent::run(download, url)
            .then(processTiles)
            .then(saveImage) Things to consider when implementing unwrapped QFutures this: Handling / propagating progress Handling errors Handling canceling and pausing

The code fails on 64-bit platforms: const QByteArray ba = ~~~ more than 4GiB of data ~~~;
const QByteArray compressed = qCompress(ba);
const QByteArray uncompressed = qUncompress(compressed);
Q_COMPARE(ba, uncompressed); It seems to be caused by qCompress() using only four digits to encode the length. There doesn't appear to be something you can do, unless you change the format to include a longer length indicator.

